# Verification log — browser-terminal prototype (Linux VM, 2026-11-13)

Environment: Linux (x86_64 VM), cargo/rustc from ~/.cargo/bin, Python 3.12 + websocket-client.

## 1. Build
Command: `cargo build --release`
Result: SUCCESS — "Finished `release` profile [optimized] target(s) in 2m 05s".
Binary: target/release/browser-terminal (3.6 MB).

## 2. HTTP auth (run A: fresh config auto-created at /tmp/bt-a/config.toml, port 17337, api_enabled=false)
- Config file was auto-created on first run with a generated token, permissions -rw------- (0600).
- `curl /` without token            -> 401
- `curl /?token=<token>`            -> 200 (UI page, <title>browser-terminal</title> present)
- `curl /` with Authorization: Bearer <token> -> 200
- `curl /?token=wrong`              -> 401
- `curl /api/sessions?token=<token>` with api_enabled=false -> 404 (API disabled)

